  "notes": [
    "The comparison is at the level of counts, gene lists and programs. No per-cell reference labels were used.",
    "Tumor IDs with an integer-valued decimal suffix (e.g. '53.0') are normalized to integer strings. Cell-type labels are matched ignoring case and surrounding whitespace; Fibroblast/CAF maps to fibroblast and Endothelial maps to endothelial cell.",
    "Undefined per-type count correlations remain null in metrics. For the count_correlation score only, they contribute zero credit; the denominator remains all seven mapped cell types other than unresolved.",
    "The paper's categories include 'unclassified' (511 cells). The agent's 'unresolved' category need not mean the same thing. Plasma cells and dendritic cells, if reported by the agent, have no counterpart in the paper's table.",
    "category_overlap is an upper bound on cell-by-cell agreement: it counts cells that could have the same category in the same tumor, not cells shown to have it.",
    "Table S3 lists are short and were selected by the paper's own method. The agent's lists are its top 60 Wilcoxon markers, so the overlap shares depend on both list lengths.",
    "Table S2 states a total of 4,645 cells, but its category counts sum to 4,644 (see reference_table_check). The comparison uses the category counts.",
    "Table S5 (cell cycle genes) was not available, so the agent's cell_cycle program is not compared. The paper reports cell cycle as a program."
